{
  "note": "The parts a track is built from beyond its sections (tracks.json): track kinds, surface patches, the ground tiles round the track and the scenery. Read by the game and by tools/track-editor.html. sectionEditor shows the section editor in the track editor: true while the game is in development, false for Final v1 (the section data and the race simulation stay the same either way). Ground and scenery art are paths under assets/art/area-map/tiled/tiles without .png; a ground's group heads it in the track editor's palette (the corner sets' edges name where the second ground is; the mixed tiles are drawn by tools/art/ground-mix.py); scenery with no art is drawn by the game. w and h are the default size on the 100 x 60 track grid. A cheer item places a cheering fan (variant, action, colour and a route they walk in by on load; cheer.ts); they stand trackside and react as bikes pass. A start_official item places the official who holds the start board, with the route they walk in the countdown (drawn in the track editor); without one the game picks their spot. official.maxWalk is the longest route allowed, in grid units (the official is about 1.3 units tall; 8 is a brisk walk in the four seconds).",
  "sectionEditor": true,
  "kinds": [
    {"id": "stadium", "name": "Stadium (supercross)", "view": "screen", "desc": "A short track in an arena that fits on one screen."},
    {"id": "outdoor", "name": "Outdoor motocross", "view": "follow", "desc": "A natural-terrain track; the view follows the riders when it is too long for one screen."},
    {"id": "endurance", "name": "Endurance", "view": "follow", "desc": "A long loop for long races; the view follows the riders, with a map of the whole track."},
    {"id": "enduro_sprint", "name": "Enduro Sprint", "view": "follow", "desc": "A timed test ridden one rider at a time, a few seconds apart, lowest total time winning. The first section is the return lane: a single-file lane from the finish line back to the start line, a quarter of the track's width, ridden at half speed and never timed."},
    { "id": "no_turn", "name": "No-Turn Takedown", "view": "follow", "desc": "A straight drag strip on a long, slim 200 × 30 grid: no bends anywhere. Four riders drop off a raised start platform and race one run to the finish line, in knockout heats after a timed seeding run, with a best-of-three final. The first section is the run-off past the finish line, where riders pull up." }
  ],
